# Consolidates author identities across ~20 years and 8 upstream repositories.
#
# xv6 began in CVS, where authors were bare usernames with no email at all
# ("rsc", "rtm", "kaashoek", "kolya"), and MIT staff later committed from many
# laptops and phone-tethered addresses. This file makes `git shortlog -sn` and
# `git blame` show one identity per person. It changes no commits.
#
# Only confident consolidations are listed: same email under different names,
# well-known CVS-era usernames, or a person's own machine-local addresses.
# Distinct contributors who merely share a surname are left alone.

